1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
TerraTwin — an open planetary analog atlas
that uses NASA data to find Earth environments
that mirror the Moon and Mars.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
We compare 12 Earth analog sites against
four planetary targets —
two on the Moon, two on Mars.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
The interactive map shows
12 Earth candidate sites.
Coordinates are provisional,
pending team confirmation.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Each site is scored against the selected target
using 8 NASA-derived features: slope, temperature,
dryness, vegetation, rock type, and more.
All scores are explicitly labeled
exploratory and provisional.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
The rankings catalogue lets you compare
all 12 sites at a glance —
filtered by group, with transparent
scoring for every site.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
TerraTwin is live at
amarahan.github.io/TerraTwin —
open-source, transparent,
and built on NASA data.
